    "title": "For the Dogs: TinCaps fall to Lugnuts on 'Paws & Claws Night' - NewsBreak",
    "text": "FORT WAYNE, Ind. (WANE) – With numerous canine friends at Parkview Field for a typical “Paws & Claws Night,” the TinCaps offense offered little bark or bite as Fort Wayne fell 8-2 to the Lansing Lugnuts. The Lugnuts outhit Fort Wayne 15-7, including registering 5 earned runs of reliever Sean Barnett in just 0.2 innings of action. Jack Costello lined an RBI single in the bottom of the third to plate Leo De Vries for Fort Wayne’s first run of the game. Jacob Campbell’s RBI ground out in the bottom of the eighth scored Oswaldo Linares for Fort Wayne’s second tally of the game. These two are set to play at Parkview Field on Thursday at 7:05 p.m. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
